"Let $X$ be an infinite set, and let $G$ be a subgroup of $S(X)$ such that $S_{\\omega}(X)\\subset G$. The topology of pointwise convergence on $G$ is the coarsest Hausdorff group topology on $G$.\n\n**Dikranjan's conjecture.** The topology of pointwise convergence is the coarsest Hausdorff group topology on $G$.\n\nThe conjecture concerns algebraically determined topologies on permutation groups. The paper confirms it by proving the stated coarseness result, so the conjecture is solved."